(Problem: Evaluate the definite integral I = int_0^{pi/2} sin^6\(x\) * cos^4\(x\) dx.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 1: Identify indices p and q:) Tj
T*
(p = 6 \(even positive integer\), q = 4 \(even positive integer\).) Tj
T*
(Since BOTH p and q are even, the multiplier factor K = pi/2.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 2: Apply Walli's formula:) Tj
T*
(Numerator terms: \(p - 1\)*\(p - 3\)*\(p - 5\) * \(q - 1\)*\(q - 3\) = \(5 * 3 * 1\) * \(3 * 1\) = 15) Tj
T*
(* 3 = 45.) Tj
T*
(Denominator terms: \(p + q\)*\(p + q - 2\)*\(p + q - 4\)... down to 2:) Tj
T*
(p + q = 10.) Tj
T*
(Denominator = 10 * 8 * 6 * 4 * 2 = 3,840.) Tj
T*
(Solution Step 3: Multiply by K = pi/2:) Tj
T*
(I = [ 45 / 3840 ] * \(pi / 2\) = [ 3 / 256 ] * \(pi / 2\) = 3*pi / 512.) Tj
T*
(Alternative Solution via Beta-Gamma Relation:) Tj
T*
(int_0^{pi/2} sin^6\(x\) * cos^4\(x\) dx = \(1/2\) * Beta\(\(6+1\)/2, \(4+1\)/2\) = \(1/2\) * Beta\(7/2,) Tj
T*
(5/2\)) Tj
T*
(= \(1/2\) * [ Gamma\(7/2\) * Gamma\(5/2\) ] / Gamma\(6\).) Tj
T*
(Gamma\(7/2\) = \(5/2\)*\(3/2\)*\(1/2\)*sqrt\(pi\) = \(15/8\)*sqrt\(pi\).) Tj
T*
(Gamma\(5/2\) = \(3/2\)*\(1/2\)*sqrt\(pi\) = \(3/4\)*sqrt\(pi\).) Tj
T*
(Gamma\(6\) = 5! = 120.) Tj
T*
(I = \(1/2\) * [ \(15/8 * 3/4 * pi\) / 120 ] = \(1/2\) * [ \(45/32 * pi\) / 120 ] = \(1/2\) * \(3*pi) Tj
T*
(/ 256\) = 3*pi / 512. \(Confirmed\).) Tj
